WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Lists, filtering and accumulation
Track the state on every iteration. total is initialized once before the loop. n receives each new number while total keeps the accumulated value.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Explanation
% computes the remainder. n % 2 == 0 selects even numbers. Only these numbers contribute to the sum. += adds to the existing value.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Trace the code
numbers = [3, 8, 5, 12, 7]
total = 0
for n in numbers:
    if n % 2 == 0:
        total += n
print(total)

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Result
20

Only 8 and 12 are even: 0 → 8 → 20. Other numbers leave total unchanged.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Remember
A common mistake is placing total = 0 inside the loop. That discards the previous sum on every iteration. Separate the input, filtering and accumulation steps.
